(function(E){ const x = E["hr-m5"] = E["hr-m5"] || {units:{}}; x.units["hr-5-1"] = {"explain":{"id":"c-hr-5-1-e","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-1","type":"explain","level":"B1","title":{"en":"Goals that work","tr":"İşe yarayan hedefler","fa":"هدف‌هایی که به نتیجه می‌رسند"},"objective":{"en":"After this lesson, you can turn vague goals into specific, measurable ones with a deadline.","tr":"Bu dersin sonunda belirsiz hedefleri son tarihi olan, somut ve ölçülebilir hedeflere dönüştürebileceksin.","fa":"بعد از این درس می‌توانی هدف‌های مبهم را به هدف‌های مشخص و قابل‌اندازه‌گیری با مهلت تبدیل کنی."},"hook":{"en":"Give every goal a number and a date. A vague goal can't be measured, so at review time it becomes an argument. 'Drive better.' Better than what? Leyla turns Omar's two vague lines into goals all three of them could score.","tr":"Her hedefe bir sayı ve bir tarih ver. Belirsiz bir hedef ölçülemez, bu yüzden değerlendirme zamanı tartışmaya dönüşür. 'Daha iyi sür.' Neye göre daha iyi? Leyla, Omar'ın iki belirsiz satırını üçünün de aynı şekilde puanlayabileceği hedeflere çeviriyor.","fa":"به هر هدف یک عدد و یک تاریخ بده. هدف مبهم قابل‌اندازه‌گیری نیست، پس موقع ارزیابی کار به بحث می‌کشد. «بهتر رانندگی کن.» بهتر از چه؟ لیلا دو جمله‌ی مبهم عمر را به هدف‌هایی تبدیل می‌کند که هر سه نفر بتوانند یکسان نمره‌شان بدهند."},"before":{"en":"Rewrite a vague work goal so that anyone can score it: what changes, by how much, by when, and why.","tr":"Belirsiz bir iş hedefini herkesin puanlayabileceği biçimde yeniden yaz: ne değişecek, ne kadar, ne zamana kadar ve neden.","fa":"یک هدف کاری مبهم را طوری بازنویسی کن که هر کسی بتواند بسنجدش: چه چیزی عوض می‌شود، چقدر، تا کی و چرا."},"rounds":[[1,4],[2,3]],"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Key points","tr":"Ana nokta","fa":"نکته‌ی اصلی"},"value":"4"},{"label":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifade","fa":"عبارت کلیدی"},"value":"5"},{"label":{"en":"Practice tasks","tr":"Alıştırma","fa":"تمرین"},"value":"4"}],"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"The skill","tr":"Beceri","fa":"مهارت"},"head":{"en":"If you can't score it, rewrite it","tr":"Puanlayamıyorsan yeniden yaz","fa":"اگر نمی‌توانی نمره بدهی، دوباره بنویس"},"body":{"en":"\"Communicate better\" means different things to different people. A working goal names what will change, by how much and by when. Then add why it matters. Now the manager and the employee can score it the same way.","tr":"\"Daha iyi iletişim kur\" herkes için başka anlama gelir. İşe yarayan bir hedef neyin, ne kadar ve ne zamana kadar değişeceğini söyler. Sonra neden önemli olduğunu ekle. Artık yönetici ve çalışan onu aynı şekilde puanlayabilir.","fa":"«بهتر ارتباط برقرار کن» برای هر کسی معنای دیگری دارد. هدف کارآمد می‌گوید چه چیزی، چقدر و تا کی تغییر می‌کند. بعد بگو چرا مهم است. حالا مدیر و کارمند می‌توانند یک جور به آن نمره بدهند."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The language","tr":"Dil","fa":"زبان"},"head":{"en":"Goal language: to + verb for purpose, by + deadline","tr":"Hedef dili: amaç için to + fiil, son tarih için by","fa":"زبان هدف‌گذاری: to برای هدف، by برای مهلت"},"steps":[{"en":"What: a number or a from-to change.","tr":"Ne: bir sayı ya da from-to değişimi.","fa":"بگو چه چیزی تغییر می‌کند: یک عدد یا تغییری از ... به ...","ex":"from six late deliveries a month to two"},{"en":"By when: by + date.","tr":"Ne zamana kadar: by + tarih.","fa":"بگو تا کی: by و تاریخ.","ex":"by 30 September"},{"en":"Why: to + verb (for + noun).","tr":"Neden: to + fiil (for + isim).","fa":"بگو چرا: to و فعل (یا for و اسم).","ex":"to improve your safety score / for safety"}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Vague","Specific and measurable"],"tr":["Belirsiz","Belirli ve ölçülebilir"],"fa":["مبهم","مشخص و قابل اندازه‌گیری"]},"rows":[["Drive better.","Reduce late deliveries from six a month to two by 30 September."],["Be careful with paperwork.","Get every delivery note signed, checked weekly, to avoid lost payments."],["Learn about safety.","Complete the defensive-driving course by 31 July to improve your safety score."]]},"tip":{"en":"Turkish için and Persian baraye work before verbs, so learners write 'for improve'. In English, purpose before a verb is to; for goes before a noun.","tr":"Türkçedeki 'için' fiillerle de kullanılır ('geliştirmek için'); bu yüzden 'for improve' yazılır. İngilizcede fiilden önce to gelir; for isimden önce gelir.","fa":"«برای» در فارسی پیش از فعل هم می‌آید («برای بهتر کردن»)؛ برای همین فارسی‌زبان‌ها می‌نویسند «for improve». در انگلیسی پیش از فعل to می‌آید و for پیش از اسم."},"wrong":"Attend the course for improve your safety score.","right":"Attend the course to improve your safety score."},{"eyebrow":{"en":"Key phrases","tr":"Anahtar ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های کلیدی"},"head":{"en":"Phrases for this task","tr":"Bu görev için ifadeler","fa":"عبارت‌های این کار"},"phrases":[{"phrase":"How will we know when...?","meaning":{"en":"Asks for a measure.","tr":"Bir ölçüt ister.","fa":"معیار سنجش را می‌پرسد."}},{"phrase":"from ... to ... by ...","meaning":{"en":"Makes a goal measurable with a deadline.","tr":"Hedefi son tarihle ölçülebilir yapar.","fa":"هدف را با یک مهلت، قابل‌اندازه‌گیری می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"What do you think is realistic?","meaning":{"en":"Invites the employee's view.","tr":"Çalışanın görüşünü sorar.","fa":"نظر خود کارمند را می‌پرسد."}},{"phrase":"measurable","meaning":{"en":"Possible to count or check.","tr":"ölçülebilir.","fa":"قابل اندازه‌گیری"}},{"phrase":"specific","meaning":{"en":"Exact and clear about one thing.","tr":"belirli, somut.","fa":"مشخص؛ دقیق"}}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"At work","tr":"İş yerinde","fa":"در محیط کار"},"head":{"en":"Ask for their own goals","tr":"Hedeflerini kendisine sor","fa":"هدف‌ها را از خودشان بپرس"},"body":{"en":"In many UK and US companies, employees are expected to suggest their own goals before the meeting. In more hierarchical workplaces, people often wait for the manager to decide and may not give their view unless asked. If you want their ideas, ask directly: \"What do you think is realistic?\"","tr":"Birçok İngiliz ve Amerikan şirketinde çalışanların toplantıdan önce kendi hedeflerini önermesi beklenir. Daha hiyerarşik işyerlerinde insanlar çoğu zaman yöneticinin karar vermesini bekler ve sorulmadıkça görüş bildirmeyebilir. Fikirlerini istiyorsan doğrudan sor: \"What do you think is realistic?\"","fa":"در بسیاری از شرکت‌های بریتانیا و آمریکا از کارمند انتظار دارند پیش از جلسه، خودش هدف‌هایش را پیشنهاد بدهد. در محیط‌های سلسله‌مراتبی‌تر، آدم‌ها اغلب منتظر می‌مانند مدیر تصمیم بگیرد و تا کسی نظرشان را نپرسد، حرفی نمی‌زنند. اگر ایده‌های آن‌ها را می‌خواهی، مستقیم بپرس: «⁨What do you think is realistic?⁩»"}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"From weak to strong","tr":"Zayıftan güçlüye","fa":"از هدف مبهم تا عدد و تاریخ"},"text":"Facts: The aim: customer emails answered within one day by 1 March, for fewer complaints.","item":"Improve customer service.","why":{"en":"Weak: nobody can score this. Strong: a number, a date and a reason.","tr":"Zayıf: bunu kimse puanlayamaz. Güçlü: bir sayı, bir tarih ve bir neden.","fa":"به نسخه‌ی اول کسی نمی‌تواند نمره بدهد. نسخه‌ی دوم یک عدد، یک تاریخ و یک دلیل دارد."},"answer":"Answer customer emails within one day by 1 March, to reduce complaints.","cut":["Improve customer service."],"cutHint":{"en":"Tap the goal that no one could score.","tr":"Kimsenin puanlayamayacağı hedefe dokun.","fa":"روی هدفی بزن که هیچ‌کس نمی‌تواند بسنجدش."}},"quick":{"prompt":"You ask an employee in a hierarchical workplace to suggest goals, and they wait for you to decide. What do you do?","options":["Ask directly: \"What do you think is realistic?\"","Set the goals yourself and move on","Tell them to send ideas by email"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Ask directly: in more hierarchical workplaces, people may not give their view unless you ask for it.","tr":"Doğrudan sor: Daha hiyerarşik iş yerlerinde insanlar sen sormadıkça görüşlerini söylemeyebilir.","fa":"مستقیم بپرس: در محیط‌های سلسله‌مراتبی‌تر، آدم‌ها ممکن است تا ازشان نپرسی نظرشان را نگویند."},"point":4},"remember":{"en":"Could you, Omar and Deniz all score this goal the same way in September? If not, add a number or a date. Result of this lesson: you can turn vague goals into measurable ones. You also have three rewritten goals.","tr":"Sen, Omar ve Deniz eylülde bu hedefi aynı şekilde puanlayabilir misiniz? Hayırsa bir sayı ya da tarih ekle. Bu dersin sonucu: belirsiz hedefleri ölçülebilir hedeflere çevirebilirsin ve elinde yeniden yazılmış üç hedef olur.","fa":"تو، عمر و دنیز می‌توانید در سپتامبر به این هدف نمره‌ی یکسانی بدهید؟ اگر نه، یک عدد یا تاریخ اضافه کن. حالا می‌توانی هدف‌های مبهم را به هدف‌های قابل‌اندازه‌گیری تبدیل کنی. سه هدف بازنویسی‌شده هم آماده است."},"b2Point":{"eyebrow":{"en":"B2 track","tr":"B2 yolu","fa":"مسیر B2"},"head":{"en":"More purpose patterns: so that, in order not to, with a view to","tr":"Daha fazla amaç kalıbı: so that, in order not to, with a view to","fa":"الگوهای بیشتر برای هدف: so that، in order not to، with a view to"},"steps":[{"en":"New subject or a full clause: so that + can / could / will.","tr":"Yeni özne ya da tam cümle: so that + can / could / will.","fa":"برای فاعل جدید یا جمله‌ی کامل، so that را با can یا could یا will به کار ببر.","ex":"We moved his start time so that he can take his niece to school."},{"en":"Negative purpose: in order not to + verb.","tr":"Olumsuz amaç: in order not to + fiil.","fa":"برای هدف منفی، in order not to و فعل را به کار ببر.","ex":"Leave early in order not to be late."},{"en":"Formal plans: with a view to + -ing.","tr":"Resmî planlar: with a view to + -ing.","fa":"در برنامه‌های رسمی، with a view to و فعل -ing‌دار می‌آید.","ex":"with a view to becoming a trainer"}],"table":{"headers":{"en":["Pattern","Example"],"tr":["Kalıp","Örnek"],"fa":["الگو","مثال"]},"rows":[["so that + clause","We moved his start time so that he can avoid the traffic."],["in order not to + verb","Leave early in order not to be late."],["with a view to + -ing","He is taking the course with a view to becoming a trainer."]]},"body":{"en":"B2 track: write one of your three goals with so that and one with in order not to or with a view to.","tr":"B2 yolu: üç hedefinden birini so that ile, birini in order not to veya with a view to ile yaz.","fa":"مسیر B2: یکی از سه هدفت را با so that و یکی را با in order not to یا with a view to بنویس."}}},"grammar":{"id":"c-hr-5-1-g","level":"B1","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-1","title":"Goal language: to + verb for purpose, by + deadline","titleTr":"Hedef dili: amaç için to + fiil, son tarih için by","exp":{"en":"A good goal says what, how much, by when and why. Two small grammar points carry most of it. Purpose: use to + base verb: \"Complete the defensive-driving course to improve your safety score.\" Turkish \"için\" and Farsi «برای» often lead learners to write \"for improve\" or \"for to improve\"; in English, for + verb is wrong here. (For is fine before a noun: \"for safety\".) Deadline: use by + time: \"Reduce late deliveries to two a month by 30 September.\" Then make the what measurable: a number, a from-to change, or something that can be checked. \"Drive better\" cannot be checked; \"from six late deliveries a month to two\" can.","tr":"İyi bir hedef ne, ne kadar, ne zamana kadar ve neden sorularını cevaplar. İki küçük dil bilgisi noktası işin çoğunu taşır. Amaç: to + yalın fiil kullan: \"Complete the defensive-driving course to improve your safety score.\" Türkçedeki \"için\" öğrencileri çoğu zaman \"for improve\" ya da \"for to improve\" yazmaya yöneltir; İngilizcede burada for + fiil yanlıştır. (İsimden önce for doğrudur: \"for safety\".) Son tarih: by + zaman kullan: \"Reduce late deliveries to two a month by 30 September.\" Sonra \"ne\"yi ölçülebilir yap: bir sayı, bir \"şundan şuna\" değişimi ya da kontrol edilebilir bir şey. \"Drive better\" kontrol edilemez; \"ayda altı gecikmeden ikiye\" edilebilir.","fa":"یک هدف خوب چهار چیز را می‌گوید: چه کاری، چقدر، تا کی و برای چه. بیشتر این بار را دو نکته‌ی کوچک دستوری به دوش می‌کشند. برای بیان منظور (برای چه)، to + فعل ساده بیاور: «⁨Complete the defensive-driving course to improve your safety score.⁩» چون در فارسی می‌گوییم «برای بهتر کردن»، فارسی‌زبان‌ها زیاد می‌نویسند «for improve» یا «for to improve»؛ اما در انگلیسی for + فعل اینجا غلط است. (قبل از اسم، for درست است: «for safety».) برای مهلت، by + زمان بیاور: «⁨Reduce late deliveries to two a month by 30 September.⁩» بعد بخشِ «چه کاری» را قابل‌اندازه‌گیری کن: یک عدد، یک تغییر «از ... به ...» یا چیزی که بشود بررسی‌اش کرد. «Drive better» قابل بررسی نیست؛ «from six late deliveries a month to two» هست."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Vague","Specific and measurable"],"tr":["Belirsiz","Belirli ve ölçülebilir"],"fa":["مبهم","مشخص و قابل اندازه‌گیری"]},"rows":[["Drive better.","Reduce late deliveries from six a month to two by 30 September."],["Be careful with paperwork.","Get every delivery note signed, checked weekly, to avoid lost payments."],["Learn about safety.","Complete the defensive-driving course by 31 July to improve your safety score."]]},"wrong":"Complete the course for improve your safety score.","right":"Complete the course to improve your safety score.","blank":{"sentence":"Attend the course ___ improve your safety score.","word":"to","distractors":["for","for to"]},"wrong2":"We want to reduce late deliveries for to save fuel.","right2":"We want to reduce late deliveries to save fuel.","blank2":{"sentence":"Reduce late deliveries to two a month ___ 30 September.","word":"by","distractors":["since","during"]},"expParts":{"tryFrom":"blank","hook":{"en":"'Drive better.' Better than what? Leyla turns Omar's two vague lines into goals all three of them could score.","tr":"'Daha iyi sür.' Neye göre daha iyi? Leyla, Omar'ın iki belirsiz satırını üçünün de aynı şekilde puanlayabileceği hedeflere çeviriyor.","fa":"«بهتر رانندگی کن.» بهتر از چه؟ لیلا دو جمله‌ی مبهم عمر را به هدف‌هایی تبدیل می‌کند که هر سه نفر بتوانند یکسان نمره‌شان بدهند."},"tryWhy":{"en":"to: purpose before a verb is to + verb. for + verb is wrong here.","tr":"to: fiilden önce amaç to + fiil ile verilir. Burada for + fiil yanlış.","fa":"جواب to است: برای بیان هدف، پیش از فعل to می‌آید. for با فعل اینجا غلط است."},"rule":[{"en":"What: a number or a from-to change.","tr":"Ne: bir sayı ya da from-to değişimi.","fa":"بگو چه چیزی تغییر می‌کند: یک عدد یا تغییری از ... به ...","ex":"from six late deliveries a month to two"},{"en":"By when: by + date.","tr":"Ne zamana kadar: by + tarih.","fa":"بگو تا کی: by و تاریخ.","ex":"by 30 September"},{"en":"Why: to + verb (for + noun).","tr":"Neden: to + fiil (for + isim).","fa":"بگو چرا: to و فعل (یا for و اسم).","ex":"to improve your safety score / for safety"}],"test":{"en":"Could you, Omar and Deniz all score this goal the same way in September? If not, add a number or a date.","tr":"Sen, Omar ve Deniz eylülde bu hedefi aynı şekilde puanlayabilir misiniz? Hayırsa bir sayı ya da tarih ekle.","fa":"تو، عمر و دنیز می‌توانید در سپتامبر به این هدف نمره‌ی یکسانی بدهید؟ اگر نه، یک عدد یا تاریخ اضافه کن."},"contrast":{"en":"Turkish için and Persian baraye work before verbs, so learners write 'for improve'. In English, purpose before a verb is to; for goes before a noun.","tr":"Türkçedeki 'için' fiillerle de kullanılır ('geliştirmek için'); bu yüzden 'for improve' yazılır. İngilizcede fiilden önce to gelir; for isimden önce gelir.","fa":"«برای» در فارسی پیش از فعل هم می‌آید («برای بهتر کردن»)؛ برای همین فارسی‌زبان‌ها می‌نویسند «for improve». در انگلیسی پیش از فعل to می‌آید و for پیش از اسم."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["for improve","for to","for reduce","for save","for become","for learn","for avoid"],"fix":{"en":"Purpose before a verb is to + verb: 'to improve your safety score'.","tr":"Fiilden önce amaç to + fiil'dir: 'to improve your safety score'.","fa":"هدف را با to و فعل بگو: «to improve your safety score»."}},{"find":["until 30 september","until the end of september","until 31 july"],"fix":{"en":"A goal deadline uses by: 'by 30 September'.","tr":"Hedef için son tarih by ile verilir: 'by 30 September'.","fa":"مهلت هدف را با by بگو: «by 30 September»."}}]},"b2":{"id":"c-hr-5-1-b2","level":"B2","track":"B2","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-1","title":"More purpose patterns: so that, in order not to, with a view to","titleTr":"Daha fazla amaç kalıbı: so that, in order not to, with a view to","exp":{"en":"B2 writers vary how they express purpose. So that + a clause (often with can, could or will) is used when the subject changes or when you need a full sentence: \"We moved his start time so that he can take his niece to school.\" In order not to + verb is the negative purpose: \"Leave ten minutes early in order not to be late.\" With a view to + -ing is formal and common in development plans: \"He is taking the course with a view to becoming a trainer.\" Traps: to in \"with a view to\" is a preposition, so it takes -ing (\"becoming\", not \"become\"); and \"in order to\" cannot be followed by a subject (\"in order to he can\" is wrong: use so that).","tr":"B2 seviyesinde yazanlar amacı farklı biçimlerde ifade eder. So that + yan cümle (çoğu zaman can, could ya da will ile), özne değiştiğinde veya tam bir cümle gerektiğinde kullanılır: \"We moved his start time so that he can take his niece to school.\" In order not to + fiil olumsuz amaçtır: \"Leave ten minutes early in order not to be late.\" With a view to + -ing resmîdir ve gelişim planlarında yaygındır: \"He is taking the course with a view to becoming a trainer.\" Tuzaklar: \"with a view to\" içindeki to bir edattır, bu yüzden -ing alır (\"become\" değil, \"becoming\"); \"in order to\"dan sonra özne gelemez (\"in order to he can\" yanlış: so that kullan).","fa":"در سطح ⁨B2⁩ منظور و هدف را به شکل‌های متنوع‌تری بیان می‌کنند. ⁨so that⁩ + جمله‌ی کامل (اغلب با ⁨can⁩، ⁨could⁩ یا ⁨will⁩) وقتی به کار می‌رود که فاعل عوض می‌شود یا به یک جمله‌ی کامل نیاز داری؛ درست مثل «برای اینکه» در فارسی: «⁨We moved his start time so that he can take his niece to school.⁩» ⁨in order not to⁩ + فعل، منظورِ منفی را می‌رساند («برای اینکه ... نشود»): «⁨Leave ten minutes early in order not to be late.⁩» ⁨with a view to⁩ + ⁨-ing⁩ رسمی است و در برنامه‌های توسعه‌ی فردی زیاد دیده می‌شود («با هدفِ»): «⁨He is taking the course with a view to becoming a trainer.⁩» دو تله: ⁨to⁩ در ⁨with a view to⁩ حرف اضافه است، پس بعدش ⁨-ing⁩ می‌آید («⁨becoming⁩»، نه «⁨become⁩»)؛ و بعد از ⁨in order to⁩ فاعل نمی‌آید («⁨in order to he can⁩» غلط است؛ به‌جایش ⁨so that⁩ بیاور)."},"formsTable":{"headers":{"en":["Pattern","Example"],"tr":["Kalıp","Örnek"],"fa":["الگو","مثال"]},"rows":[["so that + clause","We moved his start time so that he can avoid the traffic."],["in order not to + verb","Leave early in order not to be late."],["with a view to + -ing","He is taking the course with a view to becoming a trainer."]]},"wrong":"We moved his start time in order to he can avoid the traffic.","right":"We moved his start time so that he can avoid the traffic.","blank":{"sentence":"We changed the route ___ Deniz can avoid the school traffic.","word":"so that","distractors":["in order to","for"]},"wrong2":"He is taking the course with a view to become a trainer.","right2":"He is taking the course with a view to becoming a trainer.","blank2":{"sentence":"Leave ten minutes early in order ___ late.","word":"not to be","distractors":["to not being","not being"]},"useIn":{"en":"B2 track: write one of your three goals with so that and one with in order not to or with a view to.","tr":"B2 yolu: üç hedefinden birini so that ile, birini in order not to veya with a view to ile yaz.","fa":"مسیر B2: یکی از سه هدفت را با so that و یکی را با in order not to یا with a view to بنویس."},"exitItem":{"from":"hr-5-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"Start ten minutes earlier ___ miss the morning briefing.","options":["so that","in order not to","for not"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"in order not to: a negative purpose is 'in order not to' + verb. 'So that' would need a full clause, and 'for not' is not English.","tr":"in order not to: olumsuz amaç 'in order not to' + fiildir. 'So that' tam bir yan cümle ister; 'for not' İngilizce değildir.","fa":"in order not to درست است، چون هدف منفی با in order not to و فعل می‌آید. so that جمله‌ی کامل می‌خواهد و for not انگلیسی نیست."},"hint2":{"en":"The purpose is negative (not to miss it), and a base verb follows. Which option is a negative purpose before a verb?","tr":"Amaç olumsuz (onu kaçırmamak) ve ardından yalın bir fiil geliyor. Hangi seçenek fiilden önce gelen olumsuz bir amaç?","fa":"هدف منفی است (از دست ندادنش) و بعدش یک فعل ساده آمده. کدام گزینه هدفِ منفی قبل از فعل است؟"}},"expParts":{"hook":{"en":"A development plan needs more than one way to say why. Three patterns, three different jobs.","tr":"Bir gelişim planı 'neden'i söylemek için birden fazla yol ister. Üç kalıp, üç farklı görev.","fa":"در برنامه‌ی توسعه‌ی فردی، یک راه برای گفتن «چرا» کافی نیست. سه الگو، سه کار متفاوت."},"tryWhy":{"en":"not to be: the negative of in order to is in order not to + verb.","tr":"not to be: in order to'nun olumsuzu in order not to + fiil'dir.","fa":"جواب not to be است: منفیِ in order to می‌شود in order not to و فعل."},"rule":[{"en":"New subject or a full clause: so that + can / could / will.","tr":"Yeni özne ya da tam cümle: so that + can / could / will.","fa":"برای فاعل جدید یا جمله‌ی کامل، so that را با can یا could یا will به کار ببر.","ex":"We moved his start time so that he can take his niece to school."},{"en":"Negative purpose: in order not to + verb.","tr":"Olumsuz amaç: in order not to + fiil.","fa":"برای هدف منفی، in order not to و فعل را به کار ببر.","ex":"Leave early in order not to be late."},{"en":"Formal plans: with a view to + -ing.","tr":"Resmî planlar: with a view to + -ing.","fa":"در برنامه‌های رسمی، with a view to و فعل -ing‌دار می‌آید.","ex":"with a view to becoming a trainer"}],"test":{"en":"Is there a subject (he, we) after the purpose word? Then use so that, not in order to.","tr":"Amaç kelimesinden sonra bir özne (he, we) mi geliyor? O zaman in order to değil so that kullan.","fa":"بعد از کلمه‌ی هدف، فاعلی (he، we) آمده؟ پس so that بنویس، نه ⁨in order to⁩."},"contrast":{"en":"Turkish 'okula götürebilsin diye' and Persian 'ta betavanad' carry a subject easily, so learners write 'in order to he can'. English needs so that for a new subject.","tr":"Türkçede 'yeğenini okula götürebilsin diye' derken özne kolayca girer; bu yüzden 'in order to he can' yazılır. İngilizcede yeni bir özne için so that gerekir.","fa":"در فارسی می‌گوییم «تا بتواند خواهرزاده‌اش را به مدرسه ببرد» و فاعل راحت می‌آید؛ برای همین بعضی‌ها می‌نویسند «in order to he can». انگلیسی برای فاعل جدید so that می‌خواهد."}},"errorWatch":[{"find":["in order to he","in order to she","in order to we","in order to they","in order to i"],"fix":{"en":"With a subject use so that: 'so that he can avoid the traffic'.","tr":"Özneyle so that kullan: 'so that he can avoid the traffic'.","fa":"وقتی فاعل داری so that بنویس: «so that he can avoid the traffic»."}},{"find":["with a view to become","with a view to improve","with a view to take","to not being"],"fix":{"en":"with a view to takes -ing: 'with a view to becoming a trainer'.","tr":"with a view to, -ing alır: 'with a view to becoming a trainer'.","fa":"بعد از ⁨with a view to⁩ فعل ⁨-ing⁩ می‌آید: «⁨with a view to becoming a trainer⁩»."}}]},"vocab":{"id":"c-hr-5-1-v","level":"B1","category":"vocab","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-1","goals":["career"],"title":{"en":"Setting Goals","tr":"Hedef Belirlemek","fa":"هدف‌گذاری"},"cards":[{"word":"vague","sentence":"\"Drive better\" is too vague to measure.","meaning":{"en":"Not clear or exact.","tr":"belirsiz, muğlak.","fa":"مبهم؛ کلی"}},{"word":"specific","sentence":"Make each goal specific: what exactly will change?","meaning":{"en":"Exact and clear about one thing.","tr":"belirli, somut.","fa":"مشخص؛ دقیق"}},{"word":"measurable","sentence":"A measurable goal has a number in it.","meaning":{"en":"Possible to count or check.","tr":"ölçülebilir.","fa":"قابل اندازه‌گیری"}},{"word":"achievable","sentence":"Two late deliveries a month is achievable.","meaning":{"en":"Possible to reach with effort.","tr":"ulaşılabilir.","fa":"دست‌یافتنی (با تلاش قابل رسیدن)"}},{"word":"target","sentence":"The target is ninety-five per cent on time.","meaning":{"en":"A number or result you aim for.","tr":"hedef (sayısal).","fa":"هدف کمّی؛ عددی که برایش تلاش می‌کنی"}},{"word":"track","sentence":"The system tracks every delivery time.","gap":"tracks","accept":["tracks","track"],"meaning":{"en":"To follow and record progress.","tr":"izlemek, takip etmek.","fa":"پیگیری و ثبت کردن پیشرفت"}},{"word":"progress","sentence":"We'll look at your progress every month.","meaning":{"en":"Movement towards a goal.","tr":"ilerleme.","fa":"پیشرفت"}},{"word":"milestone","sentence":"The first milestone is the course on 31 July.","meaning":{"en":"An important step on the way to a goal.","tr":"ara hedef, kilometre taşı.","fa":"مرحله‌ی کلیدی؛ گام مهم در مسیر هدف"}},{"word":"KPI","sentence":"On-time delivery is our main KPI.","meaning":{"en":"Key performance indicator: a number that shows how well work is going.","tr":"temel performans göstergesi.","fa":"شاخص کلیدی عملکرد (KPI)؛ عددی که نشان می‌دهد کار چقدر خوب پیش می‌رود"}},{"word":"realistic","sentence":"Is this goal realistic with the summer traffic?","meaning":{"en":"Sensible and possible in real life.","tr":"gerçekçi.","fa":"واقع‌بینانه"}}]},"story":{"id":"c-hr-5-1-s","level":"B1","genre":"Workplace","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-1","title":{"en":"Better Than What?","tr":"Neyden Daha İyi?","fa":"بهتر از چه؟"},"text":"In July, Omar sent Leyla the goals for Deniz's next three months. There were two lines.\n\n\"1. Drive better. 2. Be more careful with paperwork.\"\n\nLeyla called him. \"How will Deniz know when he has driven better?\"\n\n\"He'll know,\" said Omar. \"I'll know.\"\n\n\"And if you disagree in September?\"\n\nOmar was quiet. He remembered the lateness week.\n\nThey set up a video call with Deniz. Leyla shared her screen. \"Let's make these goals so clear that all three of us would score them the same way.\"\n\nShe started with the first one. \"What does 'better' mean on Route 7?\"\n\n\"Fewer late deliveries,\" Omar said.\n\n\"How many now?\"\n\nOmar checked the system. \"Six last month.\"\n\n\"So: reduce late deliveries on Route 7 from six a month to two a month by 30 September. Is that realistic, Deniz?\"\n\nDeniz frowned. \"What if the traffic is bad? In August the roads near the port are terrible.\"\n\nIt was a fair question. They agreed that only delays caused by the driver would count, and that the system would show the reason for each one.\n\nThe paperwork goal became: get every delivery note signed by the customer, checked by Omar every Friday, to avoid lost payments. Then Leyla added a third goal that nobody had asked for: complete the defensive-driving course by 31 July to improve his safety score.\n\nWhen the call ended, Deniz read the three lines again. For the first time he knew exactly what a good September would look like.\n\nOmar sent one more message that evening: \"Can you do this for my other eleven drivers?\"","vocab":[{"word":"set up","en":"To arrange or organise.","tr":"ayarlamak, düzenlemek","fa":"ترتیب دادن؛ راه انداختن"},{"word":"share a screen","en":"To let others see your computer screen in a call.","tr":"ekran paylaşmak","fa":"اشتراک‌گذاری صفحه‌ی نمایش در تماس تصویری"},{"word":"frown","en":"To move your eyebrows together when worried or thinking.","tr":"kaşlarını çatmak","fa":"اخم کردن (از نگرانی یا فکر)"},{"word":"port","en":"A place where ships load and unload.","tr":"liman","fa":"بندر"},{"word":"defensive driving","en":"Driving carefully to avoid accidents caused by others.","tr":"güvenli (defansif) sürüş","fa":"رانندگی تدافعی"}],"quiz":[{"prompt":"What was wrong with Omar's first two goals?","options":["They were too hard","Nobody could check them in the same way","They had too many numbers"],"correct":1},{"prompt":"Choose the correct goal.","options":["Complete the course for improve your safety score.","Complete the course to improve your safety score.","Complete the course for to improve your safety score."],"correct":1},{"prompt":"How did they make the late-delivery goal fair?","options":["Only delays caused by the driver would count","They removed the number","Omar would decide in September"],"correct":0},{"prompt":"How did Deniz feel after the call?","options":["Confused about September","Clear about what success looked like","Angry about the extra course"],"correct":1}],"notice":{"en":"Omar's goals are two lines long. Leyla asks one question again and again. What is it, and what does it change?","tr":"Omar'ın hedefleri iki satır. Leyla tekrar tekrar bir soru soruyor. Hangisi ve neyi değiştiriyor?","fa":"هدف‌های عمر دو خط است. لیلا یک سؤال را بارها می‌پرسد. کدام سؤال و چه چیزی را عوض می‌کند؟"},"bridge":{"en":"'From six a month to two a month by 30 September.' Next: see the grammar that makes a goal measurable.","tr":"'From six a month to two a month by 30 September.' Sırada: bir hedefi ölçülebilir yapan dilbilgisini gör.","fa":"«⁨From six a month to two a month by 30 September.⁩» قدم بعد: گرامری را ببین که هدف را قابل‌اندازه‌گیری می‌کند."}},"speaking":{"id":"hr-5-1","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-1","topic":{"en":"Agreeing a Goal","tr":"Bir Hedef Üzerinde Anlaşmak","fa":"توافق بر سر یک هدف"},"warmup":{"en":"Think of a goal you once had that you never reached. Was it specific?","tr":"Bir zamanlar koyduğun ama ulaşamadığın bir hedefi düşün. Belirli miydi?","fa":"هدفی را به یاد بیاور که زمانی داشتی و هیچ‌وقت به آن نرسیدی. آیا هدف مشخصی بود؟"},"questions":[{"en":"Explain to Omar, politely, why \"drive better\" is not yet a good goal.","tr":"Omar'a \"drive better\" ifadesinin neden henüz iyi bir hedef olmadığını kibarca açıkla.","fa":"مؤدبانه به عمر توضیح بده چرا «drive better» هنوز هدف خوبی نیست."},{"en":"Propose one specific, measurable goal with a deadline (by) and a purpose (to + verb).","tr":"Son tarihli (by) ve amaçlı (to + fiil) belirli, ölçülebilir bir hedef öner.","fa":"یک هدف مشخص و قابل‌اندازه‌گیری پیشنهاد کن که مهلت (by) و منظور (to و فعل) داشته باشد."},{"en":"Deniz asks: \"What if the traffic makes me late?\" Agree how the goal will be measured fairly.","tr":"Deniz soruyor: \"Ya trafik yüzünden geç kalırsam?\" Hedefin nasıl adil ölçüleceği üzerinde anlaşın.","fa":"دنیز می‌پرسد: «⁨What if the traffic makes me late?⁩» با او توافق کن که هدف چطور منصفانه سنجیده شود."}],"followups":[{"en":"Agree the goal in 90 seconds, then 60, then 45.","tr":"Hedef üzerinde 90, sonra 60, sonra 45 saniyede anlaşın.","fa":"توافق بر سر هدف را یک بار در ۹۰ ثانیه، بعد در ۶۰ و بعد در ۴۵ ثانیه انجام بده."},{"en":"Now set one real goal for yourself this quarter: to + verb, by + a date.","tr":"Şimdi bu çeyrek için kendine gerçek bir hedef koy: to + fiil, by + tarih.","fa":"حالا برای این فصل یک هدف واقعی برای خودت بگذار: با to و فعل، و با by و تاریخ."}],"expressions":[{"phrase":"How will we know when...?","meaning":{"en":"Asks for a measure.","tr":"Bir ölçüt ister.","fa":"معیار سنجش را می‌پرسد."}},{"phrase":"from ... to ... by ...","meaning":{"en":"Makes a goal measurable with a deadline.","tr":"Hedefi son tarihle ölçülebilir yapar.","fa":"هدف را با یک مهلت، قابل‌اندازه‌گیری می‌کند."}},{"phrase":"What do you think is realistic?","meaning":{"en":"Invites the employee's view.","tr":"Çalışanın görüşünü sorar.","fa":"نظر خود کارمند را می‌پرسد."}}],"culture":{"en":"In many UK and US companies, employees are expected to suggest their own goals before the meeting. In more hierarchical workplaces, people often wait for the manager to decide and may not give their view unless asked. If you want their ideas, ask directly: \"What do you think is realistic?\"","tr":"Birçok İngiliz ve Amerikan şirketinde çalışanların toplantıdan önce kendi hedeflerini önermesi beklenir. Daha hiyerarşik işyerlerinde insanlar çoğu zaman yöneticinin karar vermesini bekler ve sorulmadıkça görüş bildirmeyebilir. Fikirlerini istiyorsan doğrudan sor: \"What do you think is realistic?\"","fa":"در بسیاری از شرکت‌های بریتانیا و آمریکا از کارمند انتظار دارند پیش از جلسه، خودش هدف‌هایش را پیشنهاد بدهد. در محیط‌های سلسله‌مراتبی‌تر، آدم‌ها اغلب منتظر می‌مانند مدیر تصمیم بگیرد و تا کسی نظرشان را نپرسد، حرفی نمی‌زنند. اگر ایده‌های آن‌ها را می‌خواهی، مستقیم بپرس: «⁨What do you think is realistic?⁩»"},"model":"Omar, 'drive better' is a good direction, but how will we know when Deniz has done it? Can we use a number? He has six late deliveries a month now. What if the goal is to reduce them from six to two by 30 September, to keep our customers? We only count delays caused by the driver, so traffic at the port does not count. What do you think is realistic?","selfCheck":[{"en":"I explained politely why the vague goal could not be measured.","tr":"Belirsiz hedefin neden ölçülemeyeceğini kibarca açıkladım.","fa":"مؤدبانه توضیح دادم چرا آن هدف مبهم قابل‌اندازه‌گیری نیست."},{"en":"My goal had a number or a from-to change.","tr":"Hedefimde bir sayı ya da from-to değişimi vardı.","fa":"هدفم یک عدد یا تغییری از ... به ... داشت."},{"en":"I gave a deadline with by and a purpose with to.","tr":"by ile bir son tarih ve to ile bir amaç verdim.","fa":"با by مهلت و با to هدف را گفتم."},{"en":"I agreed how to measure it fairly.","tr":"Nasıl adil ölçüleceği üzerinde anlaştık.","fa":"درباره‌ی اینکه چطور منصفانه اندازه‌اش بگیریم توافق کردیم."}]},"writing":{"id":"c-hr-5-1-w","title":{"en":"Three goals you can measure","tr":"Ölçülebilir üç hedef","fa":"سه هدف قابل‌اندازه‌گیری"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-1","type":"writing","difficulty":"medium","prompt":{"en":"Rewrite these three vague goals as specific, measurable goals, each with a deadline and a purpose (50-80 words): 1. Drive better. 2. Be more careful with paperwork. 3. Improve your English.","tr":"Bu üç belirsiz hedefi, her biri son tarihli ve amaçlı, belirli ve ölçülebilir hedefler olarak yeniden yaz (50-80 kelime): 1. Drive better. 2. Be more careful with paperwork. 3. Improve your English.","fa":"این سه هدف مبهم را به هدف‌هایی مشخص و قابل‌اندازه‌گیری تبدیل کن که هر کدام مهلت و منظور داشته باشد (۵۰ تا ۸۰ کلمه): 1. Drive better. 2. Be more careful with paperwork. 3. Improve your English."},"model":"1. Reduce late deliveries on Route 7 from six a month to two a month by 30 September, counting only delays caused by the driver. 2. Get every delivery note signed by the customer, checked by Omar every Friday, to avoid lost payments. 3. Complete twenty lessons of the HR English course by 31 August to handle customer calls without help.","frame":"1. Reduce ___ from ___ to ___ by ___. 2. Get every ___, checked by ___ every ___, to ___. 3. Complete ___ by ___ to ___.","words":[{"word":"by"},{"word":"to"},{"word":"from"}],"minWords":50,"minSentences":3,"rubric":["Task done: three goals, each specific, measurable, with a deadline and purpose","Organised: one goal per line, numbered","Language: to + verb for purpose; by + deadline; from ... to ...","Tone: fair and realistic, not punishing"],"rubricI18n":{"tr":["Görev: her biri somut, ölçülebilir, son tarihli ve amaçlı üç hedef","Düzen: her satırda bir hedef, numaralı","Dil: amaç için to + fiil; by + son tarih; from ... to ...","Üslup: adil ve gerçekçi, cezalandırıcı değil"],"fa":["کامل بودن کار: سه هدف، هر کدام مشخص و قابل‌اندازه‌گیری، با مهلت و منظور روشن","نظم: هر هدف در یک سطر، شماره‌دار","زبان: to با فعل برای منظور؛ by با مهلت؛ from ... to ...","لحن: منصفانه و واقع‌بینانه، نه تنبیهی"]},"portfolio":null,"parts":[{"t":{"en":"A number that changes","tr":"Değişen bir sayı","fa":"عددی که تغییر می‌کند"},"find":["from","reduce"],"sample":"late deliveries from six to two a month"},{"t":{"en":"A deadline with by","tr":"by ile bir son tarih","fa":"یک مهلت با ⁨by⁩"},"find":["by"],"sample":"by 30 September"},{"t":{"en":"A purpose with to","tr":"to ile bir amaç","fa":"یک هدف با ⁨to⁩"},"find":["to avoid","to handle","to reduce"],"sample":"to avoid lost payments"},{"t":{"en":"Who checks it","tr":"Kimin kontrol edeceği","fa":"اینکه چه کسی بررسی‌اش می‌کند"},"find":["checked by","counting only"],"sample":"checked by Omar every Friday"}]},"perspective":{"id":"c-hr-5-1-p","title":{"en":"Deniz reads his goals","tr":"Deniz hedeflerini okuyor","fa":"دنیز هدف‌هایش را می‌خواند"},"course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-1","type":"perspective","minSentences":2,"prompt":{"en":"You are Deniz reading your three new goals. Write 2-3 sentences in first person: which goal feels fair, which one worries you, and why?","tr":"Üç yeni hedefini okuyan Deniz'sin. Birinci tekil şahısla 2-3 cümle yaz: hangi hedef adil geliyor, hangisi seni endişelendiriyor ve neden?","fa":"تو دنیز هستی و سه هدف تازه‌ات را می‌خوانی. از زبان خودت دو یا سه جمله بنویس: کدام هدف به نظرت منصفانه است، کدام نگرانت می‌کند و چرا؟"}},"exit":{"id":"c-hr-5-1-x","course":"hr","unit":"hr-5-1","type":"exit","items":[{"from":"hr-5-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"Practise the new route ___ learn the shortcuts.","options":["for","to","for to"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"to: to + verb gives the purpose. 'For' + verb is wrong for purpose, and 'for to' is not English.","tr":"to: to + fiil amacı verir. Amaç için 'for' + fiil yanlıştır; 'for to' İngilizce değildir.","fa":"to درست است، چون to و فعل هدف را می‌گوید. for با فعل برای هدف غلط است و for to انگلیسی نیست."},"hint2":{"en":"The gap gives a purpose, and a base verb (learn) follows it. Which option works before a verb?","tr":"Boşluk bir amaç veriyor ve ardından yalın bir fiil (learn) geliyor. Hangi seçenek bir fiilden önce kullanılır?","fa":"جای خالی هدف را می‌گوید و بعدش یک فعل ساده (⁨learn⁩) آمده. کدام گزینه قبل از فعل می‌آید؟"}},{"from":"hr-5-1","kind":"blank","prompt":"Finish the forklift course ___ the end of March.","options":["by","since","during"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"by: 'by' + a date is a deadline. 'Since' looks back, and 'during' is the time inside a period.","tr":"by: 'by' + tarih bir son tarihtir. 'Since' geriye bakar; 'during' bir dönemin içindeki zamandır.","fa":"by درست است، چون by با تاریخ یعنی مهلت. since به عقب نگاه می‌کند و during یعنی در طول یک دوره."},"hint2":{"en":"Finishing happens once, at the latest at that time. Which word gives a deadline?","tr":"Bu, bir kez ve en geç o zamana kadar yapılacak bir iş. Hangi kelime son tarih bildirir?","fa":"تمام کردن یک بار و حداکثر تا آن زمان اتفاق می‌افتد. کدام کلمه مهلت را نشان می‌دهد؟"}},{"from":"hr-5-1","kind":"mcq","prompt":"Which goal is measurable?","options":["Drive better.","Be more careful.","Reduce late deliveries from six to two a month."],"correct":2,"point":1,"why":{"en":"'Reduce late deliveries from six to two a month' has a number you can score. 'Drive better' and 'be more careful' can't be measured.","tr":"'Reduce late deliveries from six to two a month' puanlanabilecek bir sayı içerir. 'Drive better' ve 'be more careful' ölçülemez.","fa":"«Reduce late deliveries from six to two a month» عددی دارد که می‌شود سنجید. drive better و be more careful قابل اندازه‌گیری نیستند."}},{"from":"hr-4-4","kind":"blank","prompt":"I've ___ that two route reports were missing.","options":["noticed","notice","noticing"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"noticed: 'I've' + past participle. 'Notice' and 'noticing' are not past participles.","tr":"noticed: 'I've' + üçüncü hâl. 'Notice' ve 'noticing' üçüncü hâl değildir.","fa":"noticed درست است، چون I've با اسم مفعول می‌آید. notice و noticing اسم مفعول نیستند."},"hint2":{"en":"I’ve is the start of the present perfect. Which verb form comes after have?","tr":"I’ve, present perfect’in başlangıcıdır. have’den sonra fiilin hangi biçimi gelir?","fa":"⁨I’ve⁩ شروعِ زمان حال کامل است. بعد از ⁨have⁩ فعل با چه شکلی می‌آید؟"}},{"from":"hr-4-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"Please arrive ___ 8:30 on Monday.","options":["on","at","in"],"correct":1,"point":2,"why":{"en":"at: clock times take at. 'On' is for days and dates, and 'in' is for longer periods.","tr":"at: saatler at alır. 'On' günler ve tarihler içindir; 'in' daha uzun dönemler içindir.","fa":"at درست است، چون ساعت با at می‌آید. on برای روز و تاریخ است و in برای دوره‌های طولانی‌تر."},"hint2":{"en":"8:30 is a clock time. Which word goes before a clock time?","tr":"8:30 bir saat. Saatlerden önce hangi kelime gelir?","fa":"۸:۳۰ یک ساعت است. قبل از ساعت کدام کلمه می‌آید؟"}},{"from":"hr-3-2","kind":"blank","prompt":"Tell me about a time when you ___ under pressure.","options":["worked","have worked","work"],"correct":0,"point":2,"why":{"en":"worked: 'a time when' is one finished event, so past simple. 'Have worked' links to now, and 'work' is the present.","tr":"worked: 'a time when' bitmiş tek bir olaydır, bu yüzden past simple. 'Have worked' şimdiye bağlar; 'work' şimdiki zamandır.","fa":"worked درست است، چون a time when یک اتفاق تمام‌شده است و گذشته‌ی ساده می‌خواهد. have worked به الان ربط دارد و work زمان حال است."}}]}}; })(globalThis.COURSE_FILES = globalThis.COURSE_FILES || {});
